{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775347834-VgV1a8pT5GXM849qtdIQ","role":"assistant","created":1775347844,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I see the issue. In December 1938 (file 1939_02), the table structure has combined rows. Looking at:\n- Total: 3,390 closed\n- Alcohol Tax Customs: 2,534 54 (closed)\n- Marotics.. Secret: 454 (closed)\n- Service.. Internal Revenue: 343 5 (closed)\n\nThe \"343 5\" here appears to be \"343\" for Secret Service and \"5\" for Internal Revenue. So Internal Revenue had 5 cases closed in December 1938. \n\nBut this format is different from other files where each bureau has its own row. Let me handle this edge case.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_a89426b7acbf4b42ba5b5413","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport re\n\n# Let's look at each file more carefully to handle edge cases\n# For Dec 1938, the Internal Revenue value is the second number in \"343 5\"\n\ndef extract_ir_cases_closed_v2(filepath):\n    with open(filepath, 'r') as f:\n        content = f.read()\n    \n    # Find everything between the first \"INVENTORY OF CASES\" and first \"DISPOSITIONS\"\n    inv_match = re.search(r'INVENTORY OF CASES.*?</table>', content, re.DOTALL)\n    if inv_match:\n        inv_table = inv_match.group(0)\n        \n        # Find Internal Revenue row\n        ir_match = re.search(r'Internal Revenue.*?</tr>', inv_table, re.DOTALL)\n        if ir_match:\n            row = ir_match.group(0)\n            \n            # Extract the cells\n            cells = re.split(r'</td><td', row)\n            \n            if len(cells) == 6:\n                # Normal case: separate row for Internal Revenue\n                # Cell 3 contains \"Cases closed\"\n                cell3 = cells[3]\n                num_match = re.search(r'(\\d+)', cell3)\n                if num_match:\n                    return int(num_match.group(1))\n            elif len(cells) >= 4:\n                # Combined row case (like Dec 1938 where Secret Service and Internal Revenue are in same row)\n                # The format is like \"343 5\" where 343 is Secret Service and 5 is Internal Revenue\n                # We need to find which is Internal Revenue by looking at the pattern\n                \n                # Cell 3 would be \"343 5\" - let's extract all numbers\n                numbers = re.findall(r'\\d+', cells[3])\n                if len(numbers) >= 2:\n                    # Second number is Internal Revenue\n                    return int(numbers[1])\n                elif len(numbers) == 1:\n                    return int(numbers[0])\n    \n    return None\n\n# Process all files\nfiles = [\n    (\"/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_01_page_81.txt\", \"Nov 1938\"),\n    (\"/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_02_page_111.txt\", \"Dec 1938\"),\n    (\"/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_03_page_117.txt\", \"Jan 1939\"),\n    (\"/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_04_page_95.txt\", \"Feb 1939\"),\n    (\"/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_05_page_109.txt\", \"Mar 1939\"),\n    (\"/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_06_page_117.txt\", \"Apr 1939\"),\n    (\"/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_07_page_109.txt\", \"May 1939\"),\n    (\"/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_08_page_117.txt\", \"Jun 1939\"),\n    (\"/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_09_page_66.txt\", \"Jul 1939\"),\n    (\"/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_10_page_68.txt\", \"Aug 1939\"),\n    (\"/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_11_page_70.txt\", \"Sep 1939\"),\n    (\"/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_12_page_72.txt\", \"Oct 1939\"),\n]\n\nresults = []\nfor filepath, month in files:\n    cases = extract_ir_cases_closed_v2(filepath)\n    results.append((month, cases))\n    print(f\"{month}: {cases} cases\")\n\ntotal = sum(c for _, c in results if c is not None)\nprint(f\"\\nTOTAL: {total} cases\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
