{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775347937-O1rxpxgjfQzxmDshFMiP","role":"assistant","created":1775347948,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The parsing is getting complex. Let me simplify by manually looking at each file and extracting the Internal Revenue cases closed value. Based on my earlier manual inspection of the raw output:\n\n1. Nov 1938: 20 cases\n2. Dec 1938: 5 cases (from combined row \"343 5\")\n3. Jan 1939: 12 cases \n4. Feb 1939: 13 cases\n5. Mar 1939: 11 cases\n6. Apr 1939: 16 cases\n7. May 1939: 12 cases\n8. Jun 1939: 27 cases\n9. Jul 1939: 19 cases\n10. Aug 1939: 11 cases (from second row with empty first cell)\n11. Sep 1939: 5 cases\n12. Oct 1939: 31 cases\n\nTotal: 20 + 5 + 12 + 13 + 11 + 16 + 12 + 27 + 19 + 11 + 5 + 31 = 182 cases\n\nWait, let me double check August 1939 by looking at the dispositions table as well - I may have the wrong interpretation.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_ac271eb3cc494177804f0cec","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport re\n\n# Let me try extracting from the DISPOSITIONS table instead which has cleaner data\nfor month, filepath in [\n    (\"Nov 1938\", \"/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_01_page_81.txt\"),\n    (\"Dec 1938\", \"/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_02_page_111.txt\"),\n    (\"Jan 1939\", \"/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_03_page_117.txt\"),\n    (\"Feb 1939\", \"/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_04_page_95.txt\"),\n    (\"Mar 1939\", \"/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_05_page_109.txt\"),\n    (\"Apr 1939\", \"/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_06_page_117.txt\"),\n    (\"May 1939\", \"/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_07_page_109.txt\"),\n    (\"Jun 1939\", \"/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_08_page_117.txt\"),\n    (\"Jul 1939\", \"/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_09_page_66.txt\"),\n    (\"Aug 1939\", \"/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_10_page_68.txt\"),\n    (\"Sep 1939\", \"/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_11_page_70.txt\"),\n    (\"Oct 1939\", \"/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1939_12_page_72.txt\"),\n]:\n    with open(filepath, 'r') as f:\n        content = f.read()\n    \n    # Find the Dispositions table - look for \"Number cases closed\" column with Internal Revenue\n    # Pattern: <tr><td>Internal Revenue...</td><td>XX</td> where XX is number of cases closed\n    \n    # Find the first occurrence after \"DISPOSITIONS\"\n    disp_match = re.search(r'DISPOSITIONS.*', content, re.DOTALL)\n    if disp_match:\n        disp_text = disp_match.group(0)\n        \n        # Find the row with Internal Revenue in Dispositions\n        # First try the straightforward pattern\n        match = re.search(r'Internal Revenue[^<]*</td><td>(\\d+)</td>', disp_text)\n        if match:\n            cases = int(match.group(1))\n            print(f\"{month} (disp): {cases} cases\")\n            continue\n        \n        # Try with Revenue....\n        match = re.search(r'Revenue[^<]*</td><td>(\\d+)</td>', disp_text)\n        if match:\n            cases = int(match.group(1))\n            print(f\"{month} (disp): {cases} cases\")\n            continue\n            \n    print(f\"{month}: Not found\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
