ow in August with 11 cases is indeed the Internal Revenue figure, making the 139 for Secret Service correct. The monthly totals appear consistent with this understanding.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_e3231bd020f44365bc1df5fb","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# Based on my manual verification from the raw text output:\n# The inventory tables show the following \"Cases closed\" for Internal Revenue:\n\ndata = {\n    \"Nov 1938\": 20,  # From raw: Internal Revenue</td><td>388</td><td>4</td><td>20</td>\n    \"Dec 1938\": 5,   # From raw: Service.. Internal Revenue</td>...<td>343 5</td> - second number is IR\n    \"Jan 1939\": 12,  # From raw: Internal Revenue..</td><td>379</td><td>4</td><td>12</td>\n    \"Feb 1939\": 13,  # From raw: Internal Revenue...</td><td>371</td><td>61</td><td>13</td>\n    \"Mar 1939\": 11,  # From raw: Internal Revenue...</td><td>419</td><td>13</td><td>11</td>\n    \"Apr 1939\": 16,  # From raw: Internal Revenue...</td><td>421</td><td>9</td><td>16</td>\n    \"May 1939\": 12,  # From raw: Internal Revenue</td><td>414</td><td>6</td><td>12</td>\n    \"Jun 1939\": 27,  # From raw: Internal Revenue...</td><td>408</td><td>14</td><td>27</td>\n    \"Jul 1939\": 19,  # From raw: Internal Revenue</td><td>395</td><td>20</td><td>19</td>\n    \"Aug 1939\": 11,  # From raw: empty row after Secret Service - Second number is for IR\n    \"Sep 1939\": 5,   # From raw: Revenue....</td><td>405</td><td>52</td><td>5</td>\n    \"Oct 1939\": 31,  # From raw: Internal Revenue...</td><td>452</td><td>33</td><td>31</td>\n}\n\nprint(\"Internal Revenue Cases Closed in US District Courts\")\nprint(\"(November 1938 to October 1939)\")\nprint(\"=\" * 55)\ntotal = 0\nfor month, cases in data.items():\n    print(f\"{month}: {cases:>3} cases\")\n    total += cases\nprint(\"=\" * 55)\nprint(f\"TOTAL: {total} cases\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
